The reverse DCF (9/15/2026) estimated a share price of $57.20 for COHR compared to a current price (as of 9/15/2026 at 
7:56:50) of $271.17 per share. Our predicted share price is around 5 times less than the actual price stock 
price of the company. This could be attributed to a number of reasons including our assumptions in the DCF implying 
less future cash flow than market price seems to anticipate, growth sharply slowing down (40.5% -> 15% -> 10% ->
6% -> 3% over the next 5 years), a substantial investment (capital expenditures and working capital consume
significant cash), and WACC still being a placeholder. Our assumptions of growth, margin, and reinvestment 
have a major impact on the forecast. Our forecast does not prove that COHR is overpriced; rather, it shows 
that we need to do further research into the company's future opportunities and market expectations of strong
results. 

